From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:41:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] tu: Don't request mid-submission preemption

On the Adreno X1-85 a switch in the middle of a submission loses work in
flight. Leave MSM_SUBMITQUEUE_ALLOW_PREEMPT off unless TU_ALLOW_PREEMPT is
set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
index 2f4bcf1..6e35dff 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
@@ -1404,7 +1404,8 @@ tu_knl_drm_msm_load(struct tu_instance *instance,
    device->has_raytracing = tu_drm_get_param_or(fd, MSM_PARAM_RAYTRACING, &val, false);
    device->has_sparse_prr = tu_drm_get_param_or(fd, MSM_PARAM_HAS_PRR, &val, false);
 
-   device->has_preemption = msm_common_has_preemption(device->local_fd, device->submitqueue_priority_count / 2);
+   device->has_preemption = os_get_option("TU_ALLOW_PREEMPT") &&
+                            msm_common_has_preemption(device->local_fd, device->submitqueue_priority_count / 2);
 
    device->is_perf_cntr_selectable = true;
 
